A reload that bypasses the HTTP cache fetches the document with the
“reload” cache mode in Ladybird. And until the document has completely
loaded, so do its requests still in the “default” mode, and the
navigations of its child navigables.

Blink does the same. NavigationRequest gives a RELOAD_BYPASSING_CACHE
navigation net::LOAD_BYPASS_CACHE, which skips reading the HTTP cache
but still writes it. And for a kReloadBypassingCache load, Blink’s
DetermineFrameCacheMode() returns kBypassCache until the document’s
LoadEventFinished() — a mode that PrepareResourceRequestForCacheAccess()
applies only to requests still in kDefault. And HTMLFrameOwnerElement
gives a child frame’s load kReloadBypassingCache while its parent’s is.

WebKit’s FrameLoader::reload() makes the load ReloadFromOrigin, for
which FrameLoader::subresourceCachePolicy() returns CachePolicy::Reload
until the frame’s load completes, a child frame taking its parent’s
policy. CachedResourceRequest::updateCacheModeIfNeeded() applies that
only to requests in the default cache mode. Its plain reload already
ignores the cache for the document itself: FrameLoader::reload() sets
ReloadIgnoringCacheData for every reload.

Gecko’s skip-cache reload gives the document channel nsIRequest::
LOAD_BYPASS_CACHE in nsDocShellLoadState::CalculateChannelLoadFlags(),
and nsLoadGroup passes it on to every channel the document’s load group
adds. And nsDocShell::MaybeHandleSubframeHistory() gives a child
docshell its parent’s force-reload load type. But Ladybird doesn’t
follow Gecko in two respects: The load group keeps the flag after the
load ends, so a late fetch() bypasses the cache too. And each channel
gets the flag ORed into its own, so a request that names a cache mode
bypasses the cache anyway.

Blink and Gecko also skip service workers for such a reload; Ladybird
doesn’t run a service worker’s fetch handling at all yet. And all three
engines fetch a URL only once per load, where Ladybird fetches the URL
of each script or stylesheet element on its own (its images already
share one request per document).
